WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.133 --> 00:00:02.400
-I want to get serious...
-What?

00:00:02.400 --> 00:00:04.467
-...for a s--
No, I don't.

00:00:04.467 --> 00:00:06.133
How could I ever get serious
after that?

00:00:06.133 --> 00:00:08.467
Alright, guys, I love everyone's
in the partying mode.

00:00:08.467 --> 00:00:10.400
-It's Friday party.
-Oh, it's Friday.

00:00:10.400 --> 00:00:11.667
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Today's Friday?

00:00:11.667 --> 00:00:13.200
-Friday.

00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:14.334
Oh, shoot.

00:00:14.334 --> 00:00:15.734
-Today's Friday.
-It is Friday.

00:00:15.734 --> 00:00:17.300
-Usually on Friday,
I check my inbox, of course.

00:00:17.300 --> 00:00:18.534
-What else do you do?
-I return some e-mails,

00:00:18.534 --> 00:00:20.300
and I write out
thank you notes every Friday.

00:00:20.300 --> 00:00:21.634
-Really?
-I'm running late.

00:00:21.634 --> 00:00:23.367
Do you guys mind?

00:00:23.367 --> 00:00:25.367
Do you guys mind
if I write 'em out right now?

00:00:25.367 --> 00:00:26.634
Is that okay during the show?

00:00:26.634 --> 00:00:28.334
[ Cheers and applause ]
I understand.

00:00:28.334 --> 00:00:29.801
I appreciate this.

00:00:29.801 --> 00:00:31.834
James, can I get some thank
you note writing music, please?

00:00:31.834 --> 00:00:35.968
[ Piano rendition of
"Celebration" plays ]

00:00:35.968 --> 00:00:37.567
-♪ Whoo-hoo ♪

00:00:37.567 --> 00:00:39.434
[ Laughter ]

00:00:39.434 --> 00:00:41.567
-[ Laughing ] God.

00:00:41.567 --> 00:00:44.033
What is going --

00:00:44.033 --> 00:00:46.467
Like a baby -- That was
a lullaby Kool &amp; The Gang.

00:00:46.467 --> 00:00:49.601
It was like, "Alright.
Go to sleep, everybody."

00:00:49.601 --> 00:00:52.100
[ Laughter ]

00:00:52.100 --> 00:00:53.534
[ Piano rendition of
"Celebration" plays ]

00:00:53.534 --> 00:00:56.033
-Alright, shh!

00:00:56.033 --> 00:00:58.033
-Whoo-hoo!

00:00:58.033 --> 00:01:00.667
-Shh-shh!

00:01:00.667 --> 00:01:02.734
That's the most excited
I've ever seen James.

00:01:03.767 --> 00:01:05.133
♪♪

00:01:05.133 --> 00:01:08.067
-Thank you,
Travis and Jason Kelce,

00:01:08.067 --> 00:01:09.968
for being two brothers
wearing red and green,

00:01:09.968 --> 00:01:12.467
making you the Mario and Luigi
of the NFL.

00:01:12.467 --> 00:01:14.868
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:14.868 --> 00:01:16.501
-Yeah, come on.

00:01:18.701 --> 00:01:20.234
"It's-a me, Travis."

00:01:20.234 --> 00:01:22.133
[ Laughter ]

00:01:22.133 --> 00:01:23.334
♪♪

00:01:23.334 --> 00:01:25.734
-Thank you, the word
"tailgate,"

00:01:25.734 --> 00:01:28.267
for being a parking lot party
but also sounding like the name

00:01:28.267 --> 00:01:30.033
of a Trump scandal
we never got to.

00:01:30.033 --> 00:01:34.133
He's like, "I've got nothing
to do with tailgates."

00:01:34.133 --> 00:01:36.000
-"There's a lot of tail" --
-"I was not even --

00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:37.801
I wasn't even there
for tailgates."

00:01:37.801 --> 00:01:39.534
[ Light laughter ]

00:01:39.534 --> 00:01:40.901
♪♪

00:01:40.901 --> 00:01:42.734
Thank you, US military,

00:01:42.734 --> 00:01:45.133
for shooting down
China's spy balloon.

00:01:45.133 --> 00:01:46.534
I just feel bad for the guy

00:01:46.534 --> 00:01:48.601
who spent six months
blowing it up.

00:01:48.601 --> 00:01:50.701
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:53.767 --> 00:01:55.567
[ Balloon deflates ]

00:01:55.567 --> 00:01:57.767
The whole time, I wasn't
squeezing it to get the air.

00:01:57.767 --> 00:01:58.868
The --

00:02:00.634 --> 00:02:02.033
♪♪

00:02:02.033 --> 00:02:06.200
Thank you, entire Super Bowl
stadium made out of snacks,

00:02:06.200 --> 00:02:08.200
for being an impressive way
to show your friends

00:02:08.200 --> 00:02:11.200
that you love football
and have way too much free time.

00:02:11.200 --> 00:02:12.901
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:12.901 --> 00:02:15.234
"...and pretzels
and carrots.

00:02:15.234 --> 00:02:16.467
Celery's there."

00:02:16.467 --> 00:02:18.000
-[ Nasally ] This soppressata
represents --

00:02:18.000 --> 00:02:19.567
-[ Nasally ] What I do
is I take a Dorito

00:02:19.567 --> 00:02:21.200
and put it
inside of a pretzel.

00:02:21.200 --> 00:02:22.534
-Well, I use pretzel man as --

00:02:22.534 --> 00:02:24.200
-And I dip the whole pretzel
in the nacho --

00:02:24.200 --> 00:02:25.701
the the nacho cheese.
It says --

00:02:25.701 --> 00:02:27.100
-Really?
-Yeah, it's pretty funny.

00:02:27.100 --> 00:02:28.734
Well, you get the nacho cheese
to a certain temperature,

00:02:28.734 --> 00:02:31.534
And it will melt, of course,
and then cool off.

00:02:31.534 --> 00:02:33.100
-Yeah, it will solidify
a different way,

00:02:33.100 --> 00:02:34.100
making a different texture.

00:02:34.100 --> 00:02:35.601
-Yeah, so it starts as a liquid.

00:02:35.601 --> 00:02:38.033
Ends up a solid in your mouth,
then it becomes a liquid again.

00:02:38.033 --> 00:02:40.100
-I know, exactly.
Then it ends up as a gas.

00:02:40.100 --> 00:02:42.367
[ Laughter ]

00:02:44.667 --> 00:02:46.133
[ Normal voice ] Celebrate good
times, you know what I mean?

00:02:46.133 --> 00:02:48.501
-[ Normal voice ] Mm-hmm.

00:02:48.501 --> 00:02:49.501
♪♪

00:02:49.501 --> 00:02:52.234
Thank you,
the City of Philadelphia.

00:02:52.234 --> 00:02:54.334
Win or lose,
it was nice knowing you.

00:02:54.334 --> 00:02:56.400
Yeah. Good luck.

00:02:56.400 --> 00:02:58.334
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:58.334 --> 00:02:59.801
-Come on.
Please don't --

00:02:59.801 --> 00:03:03.000
-Come on, come on. Philly,
come on, Philly.

00:03:03.000 --> 00:03:04.067
Please.
-"You got a hoagie" --

00:03:04.067 --> 00:03:06.801
-Please keep it cool.
Come on, guys.

00:03:06.801 --> 00:03:08.234
♪♪

00:03:08.234 --> 00:03:12.367
Thank you, Doritos spending
$7 million on Super Bowl ads,

00:03:12.367 --> 00:03:14.834
for vastly overestimating
the amount of effort

00:03:14.834 --> 00:03:17.133
it takes to get me
to buy Doritos.

00:03:17.133 --> 00:03:19.801
I love Doritos.

00:03:19.801 --> 00:03:22.000
-More?
-I'm good.

00:03:22.000 --> 00:03:23.400
-Wait, you know what?

00:03:23.400 --> 00:03:25.000
-They're part
of a balanced meal.

00:03:25.000 --> 00:03:26.400
-Maybe I should get
some Doritos.

00:03:26.400 --> 00:03:27.501
Hadn't thought about it.
-I have them in the morning

00:03:27.501 --> 00:03:29.067
in a bowl with milk, yeah.

00:03:29.067 --> 00:03:30.968
[ Laughter ]

00:03:30.968 --> 00:03:32.267
♪♪

00:03:32.267 --> 00:03:35.734
Thank you,
Chiefs mascot KC Wolf.

00:03:35.734 --> 00:03:37.934
I'm not sure what a raccoon
on bath salts

00:03:37.934 --> 00:03:39.467
has to do
with football or Chiefs,

00:03:39.467 --> 00:03:41.100
but I'm willing to go for it.

00:03:41.100 --> 00:03:43.033
[ Cheers and applause ]
I love it.

00:03:43.033 --> 00:03:46.467
[ Shrieking ]

00:03:46.467 --> 00:03:49.400
"Football!"
-[ Laughs ]

00:03:49.400 --> 00:03:51.567
-Sandler's the mascot?
-[ As Adam Sandler ] Yes!

00:03:51.567 --> 00:03:54.100
[ Laughter ]

00:03:54.100 --> 00:03:55.601
-[ Chuckles ]

00:03:55.601 --> 00:03:57.367
-Aw, is this the last one?
-Yeah.

00:03:57.367 --> 00:03:59.234
[ Laughter ]

00:03:59.234 --> 00:04:01.200
-This is the final --
This is the final one?

00:04:01.200 --> 00:04:04.167
-Thank you, "Last of Us" zombie,

00:04:04.167 --> 00:04:06.234
for looking like
that one weird chicken wing

00:04:06.234 --> 00:04:07.701
on the tray that no one eats.

00:04:07.701 --> 00:04:09.467
There you have it, everybody.
Those are our thank you notes.

